WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.850
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.310
Strike out!

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.730
You did it!

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.660
The Bats have finally gotten to first place in the Eastern Division!

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.450
Shigeno recorded his 19th save!

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.490
That's exactly what I'd expect from you,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.410
Goro-kun.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.590
Hello, this is Sato.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.160
This is Araki.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.670
Coach Araki.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.330
Could you stop by the coach's office for a bit?

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.350
Sato.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.690
Put on the starter's mask tomorrow.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.240
Yes, sir!

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.820
Yatabe said that his hip isn't feeling good.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.120
I want him to rest tomorrow.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.600
I'm expecting great things from you,

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.790
Golden Rookie.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:10.960
Yes, sir!

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.010
Excuse me.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.650
<i>Goro-kun...</i>

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.070
<i>I won't lose either!</i>

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.860
All right!

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.010
It's finally time for the game against the number one team in runs: the Rockets!

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.660
We'll win with a bang, and then we'll be on our way to the championship at full speed!

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.010
Yeah!

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:50.410
At this rate, we'll win by a wide margin and make the playoffs!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.460
You idiot!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.910
Every year, we go into a lull in the summer and lose our grasp on victory!

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.670
Don't forget that we need to concentrate on every single game!

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.630
We know that!

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.420
You're noisy, Sergeant.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.490
What do you mean by "you're noisy"!?

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:06.730
If you idiots play badly, I won't forgive you!

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.880
Hey, damn you! Are you listening?

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.880
Hey, everyone!

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:09.770
Do you have a minute?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.800
Allow me to introduce a new member.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:20.900
He's been promoted from Double A today.
 This is the newcomer, Keane.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.820
You guys should know about him too.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:32.580
He was drafted number one by our Indiana Hornets this year;

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.980
he's the golden rookie catcher!

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:38.590
In no time at all, he's already risen to Triple A!

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.380
<i>This guy's a catcher, huh?</i>

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.490
Nice to meet you, rookie!

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.610
Nice to meet you.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.080
We've heard the rumors about you.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.800
You're supposed to have an incredible throwing arm.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.970
<i>Golden rookie, eh?</i>

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.900
So then, I'm sorry, Sanders.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.860
I'll have you moved to the bench.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.250
Keane is a golden egg.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:04.940
I've been told directly by the Hornets' General Manager...

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:11.700
to build up his experience in real games and prepare him carefully for the Majors.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:15.050
Since you've got tons of experience,

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.000
make sure to thoroughly advise him however you can!

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.250
You got it, right?

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.920
Yes, sir.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.550
Becoming a bench player after making it all the way here...

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.820
What a pity, Sergeant.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.380
Don't say that.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.520
In this world, it can happen to anyone.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:00.380
Yo, Keane!

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.150
Um, well, I was thinking...

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.630
I thought that maybe I should explain a little...

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.550
about Carlisle, the starting pitcher today.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.590
He's a pitcher with lots of bad habits, but...

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.200
if you can get the knack of him, it'll work out.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.810
I'll get the knack of controlling him.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.390
Excuse me.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:22.060
I have a lot of things that I need to do before the game.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.900
What's with him?

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.340
Out!

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:51.840
Strike out!

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:56.930
Out!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.330
Amazing!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:02.300
The starting pitcher, Carlisle, is in really good shape right from the start today!

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.280
He's in good shape thanks to Keane.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.360
So that's it!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:11.780
He's pulling out Carlisle's strong points! It's what's to be expected!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.710
Ball!

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.330
Out!

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.050
You did it!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.300
Incredible, incredible!

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.430
I'm surprised!

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.710
What an amazing arm he's got!

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.050
Ball! Ball four!

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:54.320
Now hitting, number 7: Jeff Keane!

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:57.820
Play!

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:18.470
You did it!

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.350
Three-run homer!

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.250
Hey, hey, that rookie is too amazing!

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:28.190
Showing up with all that hype wasn't for nothing.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.960
Even if I'm not in there,

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.740
if the team can win, then that's enough.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.500
Attention please, pitching, number 56:

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:51.010
Goro Shigeno!

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.070
Goro! Go, Goro!

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.680
It's the Bats' expectation-ladened rookie battery!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.170
You...

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.060
seem to only have fastballs.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:54.220
Yeah, so you don't need to do any signs or pre-battle strategies.

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.490
It's enough if you point approximately where I should throw. {Kohn: I'm not 100% sure of this one, maybe it's slightly  off...}

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.590
I don't know how you've been doing things up till today, but...

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:03.910
I'll have you pitch according to my lead today.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.370
Even if you only have fastballs,

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.290
if you pitch according to how I say, I can figure something out.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.080
What was that?

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.250
Hey!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:22.640
<i>That bastard! Even though he's a newcomer, he's got such a big mouth!</i>

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.310
Now hitting, number 8: Fisher!

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.060
Play!

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.410
<i>It doesn't matter if it's a ball.</i>

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.980
<i>Throw it outside.</i>

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.010
<i>You're annoying.</i>

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.280
<i>Despite how I look,</i>

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.700
<i>I've piled up 19 saves. I'm the Bats'...</i>

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.990
<i>guardian deity, don't you know!</i>

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.540
Oh no!

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.960
No outs and a runner on first!

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.500
Damn it! He was aiming for it!

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:59.090
I told you to pitch it outside,
so why did you pitch it inside?

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.150
If you can't pitch according to my lead,

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:07.220
then either you or I need to step down.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.600
W-What?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.170
W-What?

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:16.440
This is a free fansub.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:16.440
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:24.830
Are you going to pitch according to my lead or not?

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.780
Which is it?

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.120
If you aren't,

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.830
then I don't need to catch your pitches.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.740
Then one of us will just go to the bench.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.050
What kind of bullshit are you talking, punk?

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.220
I don't know anything about you being a golden rookie or whatever,

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.680
but I've got my own way of doing things!

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:50.520
Who was the one who allowed a runner on with no outs by doing things his own way?

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:55.630
Number 2, Fisher, takes his time if there's a runner,

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:59.940
but if there aren't any runners, he's the type to swing at the first pitch.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:03.520
Also, according to the stats, he's strong against inside pitches.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.190
To think that you'd...

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:08.990
immediately ignore my instructions...

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.410
and use an ill-advised inside pitch...

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:16.910
In the first place, you don't have the numbers to be convincing.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.420
Numbers?

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.490
Goro Shigeno.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.050
Two wins, three losses, 19 saves.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:27.260
The number of saves is good, I'll give you that, but your earned run average is 3.26.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.510
Your opponent's batting average is .370.

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:33.180
If you compare them with closers on other baseball teams,

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.740
they aren't numbers to brag about.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:38.280
The only thing you can brag about is...

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:41.420
your strike out ratio of 13.25 per nine.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.820
Why you!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.320
How can you know all that when you were just promoted to Triple A today!?

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:52.160
I got it from the score sheets, isn't that obvious?

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:53.830
Well...

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.860
I have the stats memorized...

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.680
of the important players in this league, at least.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.300
Furthermore,

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:04.310
I inputted the stats of all the players from both teams before the game...

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:07.010
and analyzed it myself.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:07.970
As a result,

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:15.830
today's starting pitcher, Carlisle, managed to go all the way to the eighth inning without giving up a run because of my lead.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:18.740
Hey!

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:19.900
What are you doing?

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.870
Don't just stand there and babble forever!

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.380
I'm sorry, I'll return now.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.390
If you understand,

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.620
pitch according to my lead.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:34.860
If by a one in a million chance you get hit,

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.860
I'll take all the responsibility.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.220
Now hitting, number 3: Cervantes.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:49.970
Play!

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:54.790
No outs and a runner on first base with a three-run lead...

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.020
Shigeno-kun, do your best!

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:04.710
<i>This guy has a batting average of .300, but...</i>

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.740
<i>he's been having trouble with pitches that are low this season.</i>

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:09.160
<i>For the first pitch,</i>

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.830
<i>throw it low and inside!</i>

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:13.870
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.430
<i>I've formed a battery with Toshiya, Komori,</i>

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:20.540
<i>and many other catchers up till now, but...</i>

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:25.050
<i>this is the first time I've been with such a single-minded and annoying catcher!</i>

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:29.940
<i>I don't know how important you say stats are, but...</i>

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:32.390
<i>Sanders does a way better job as a catcher than you!</i>

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:35.890
Ball!

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:39.890
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:40.940
<i>So that's how you'll play.</i>

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.310
That was dangerous!

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:45.230
Yet another pitch against the lead!

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.820
<i>We've got a three-run lead.</i>

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.280
<i>Don't be petty and selfish about how you want to lead!</i>

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.180
What are you doing, Keane?

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:04.790
Hurry and go pick it up!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.510
Did he lose sight of the ball?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.840
Why, you!

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.360
Geez, what are they doing?

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.970
Damn it!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.700
You bastard!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.990
You didn't catch it on purpose, right?

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:41.920
In what world does the catcher allow a passed ball on purpose?

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:46.280
Throw it to the place that I say.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:48.660
If you do that,

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:49.970
I'll catch it.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:50.970
Y-You!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.380
Y-You!

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.400
Hey, you two!

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.710
W-What are you two doing?

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:56.430
Stop it!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.270
What are the rookies fighting over?

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:06.230
That married couple is getting hot already!

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:08.780
I see.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:10.300
I got it.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.700
Then let's do this.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:16.700
For the time being, I'll pitch according to your commands.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.700
If you can get us through this inning without any earned runs being scored,

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.950
then I will listen to everything you say without complaining from now on.

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:28.130
But if you let them score even one run,

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.330
never try to give me orders again!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.530
No, rather,

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.010
when I'm pitching, turn the catcher's mask...

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:36.470
over to Sanders!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.020
I'll never form a battery with you again.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:42.370
W-What are you saying, Shigeno?

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.410
That's not something you guys can deci-

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.650
Very well.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:50.980
I also refuse to work with a monkey who doesn't listen to the catcher and acts like he's the boss.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.850
And you, if you lose this bet,

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:57.530
never talk back to me again.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:07.020
There are only three more outs left; why are you dawdling!?

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:08.870
Hurry up and end this!

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.380
Go, Goro!

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:14.340
Play!

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:20.950
<i>I successfully fooled him into accepting those bad terms.</i>

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:23.390
<i>It's the clean-up hitter with no outs and a runner on third.</i>

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:28.560
<i>No matter who's pitching, the probability that the opponents will score is high!</i>

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:32.820
<i>Well then, what kind of pitch are you going to request?</i>

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:40.530
What?

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:41.620
He's walking him!?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.330
<i>This guy...</i>

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.180
<i>What in the world is he thinking?</i>

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.290
<i>I'm not responsible for this!</i>

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.050
Ball!

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.870
Ball! Ball four!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:03.430
Now hitting, number 9: Aaron.

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:04.540
<i>I-I don't get this.</i>

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.040
<i>I-I don't get this.</i>

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:10.010
<i>Even if he made a bet with Shigeno, there's a three-run difference!</i>

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:12.020
<i>If you concentrate on winning the game,</i>

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:16.330
<i>you shouldn't bother with whether the runner on third scores or not.</i>

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.860
<i>I don't see the meaning in amassing runners...</i>

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:22.080
<i>Consecutive walks!?</i>

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:23.670
Wait a minute!

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:25.920
What's he thinking?

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.600
Intentionally putting the tying runner on base...

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:29.620
What is he doing?

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.430
What's with him!?

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.790
I've never heard of such an absurd tactic!

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:48.980
Stop screwing around!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.150
<i>It can't be that...</i>

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:59.100
<i>because of his bet with me he's trying this sink-or-swim tactic?</i>

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.240
Time, time!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.660
You bastard!

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:06.450
Let's stop this!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.210
Let's stop this stupid bet!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:11.120
You intend to throw away the game just because of one run?

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:14.190
What are you talking about?

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:18.380
I'm not planning on throwing away the game.

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.590
What?

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:21.470
Anyway, do as I say until the end.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.510
If you stop here,

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:24.800
the plan will be ruined.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.500
What are those two talking about?

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:32.600
That's what I want to ask!

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.370
Ball! Ball four!

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.450
<i>What do you mean, "plan"? I'm not responsible for this!</i>

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.730
<i>I don't understand this.</i>

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:48.790
<i>I've never heard of such a plan.</i>

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:52.470
Come on, this is bad for business!

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:56.090
If we lose here, the customers will be mad!

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:01.240
<i>That Keane... What is he planning?</i>

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.850
Now hitting, number 2: Bennett.

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:15.830
Damn it!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.610
You're underestimating me!

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:19.830
Play!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:24.600
He's really pumped up!

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:29.630
If he hits a big one, they'll take the lead.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.710
Come on, you brat!

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.100
<i>Number 3, Cervantes, is a .300 hitter.</i>

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.850
<i>Number 4, Aaron, has a batting average of .400 with runners in scoring position.</i>

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.050
<i>If we're going to challenge them,</i>

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:48.220
<i>it's got to be him, number 5!</i>

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:53.520
<i>He's an archetypical clumsy and selfish long distance "cannon."</i>

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:59.690
<i>And he's got such a short temper that he's been ejected four times in three years.</i>

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:03.930
<i>He hits .190 with runners in scoring position.</i>

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:08.120
<i>Also, he's gone one for ten with the bases loaded this season,</i>

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.160
<i>and...</i>

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.410
<i>his batting average against pitches low and inside is...</i>

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.080
<i>no more than .067!</i>

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:18.870
<i>And he just saw us walk the two before him to load the bases...</i>

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.380
<i>to challenge him.</i>

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:25.720
<i>The likelihood that he'll hit the runners home, strained with anger,</i>

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:30.010
<i>is almost exactly zero!</i>

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.060
Back home!

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.800
Out!

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:37.600
Out!

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:38.650
To first!

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:43.280
Out! Out!

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:45.580
Game over!

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:53.620
Amazing!

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.190
<i>A triple play... seriously?</i>

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:07.680
<i>A triple play... seriously?</i>

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.110
This is unbelievable!

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:11.550
It can't be...

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:14.750
He can't have been aiming for the triple play the whole time.

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:17.190
You did it!

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:18.170
Triple play!

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.270
Yay!

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:20.770
That was too awesome!

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:26.190
I won the bet.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:29.570
Never disobey me again.

00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:14.480
Thanks to Keane, the Bats continue moving forward.

00:24:14.480 --> 00:24:17.310
It's true that your statistical baseball is incredible.

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:18.300
But...

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:19.390
we pitchers...

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:21.770
aren't your tools!

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:23.420
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:24.810
Keane's Past.

00:24:25.300 --> 00:24:27.620
Run to the stage of your dreams!
